# Kandelo patch rationale (S19)
#
# Node installs native data properties on objects that already exist.
# Replacing an object with a proxy changes identity; replacing a data property
# with a getter changes its descriptor. Keep those engine semantics. The
# bridge now owns the callback record, traced realm/payload and finalizer;
# the engine reads only a generic immutable dispatch table. Its original
# property algorithms still control caching, reentry and failure behavior.
#
# Source-only cleanup; not rebuilt or behavior-qualified. Retention remains
# subject to README.md: Future work: platform omissions.

